WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.460
Hello, my beautiful witches and warlocks, it's time for
a new episode of "American Horror Story: Apocalypse".

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.420
So fill up your tank and prepare for
biology class, because this one's a doozy.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:17.320
Cordelia wakes up among the burned ashes of Robichaux's Academy for Exceptional Young Ladies.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:23.220
It seems everything around her has fallen to a
nuclear blast, but miraculously, she's still alive.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.780
But things get worse for Cordelia: she's
surrounded by ravenous mutated cannibals.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:33.480
She tries to use her powers but they don't seem to work, eventually being overcome by the horde and ripped apart

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:38.440
as Michael Langdon, wearing his sexy
demonic old man face, laughs maniacally.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.620
But then we realized it was all a dream.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.860
She wakes up and we're in the past
timeline, the one where she fainted at the end.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.080
Remember, there are currently two timelines:

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.940
Present day, where Michael has taken over the Outpost,

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.320
and past, where Michael has
returned with Madison and Queenie.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.840
In her dream, Cordelia called out all
her witchy sisters except for Madison,

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.160
and of course, she had to say something about it.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:04.360
She has a brief moment to hug her friends
and then says she wants to see the boy,

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.480
referring to Michael.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.700
But as we'll find out, Cordelia
doesn't think this was a dream.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:13.940
It's an omen of the future, of the impending
rise of Michael and the apocalypse to come.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:18.500
And if this is indeed a vision, what of
Cordelia's inability to use her power?

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.520
We do learn later in this episode her powers are fading.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.060
Will this come true later on?

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.900
And is her death in the vision
an omen of things to come?

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:30.440
The witches and warlocks meet and Cordelia
admits she's impressed with Michael's skills.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:36.400
Cordelia tells them her dream was a vision of
the future. It's filled with cataclysm, fire, death.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.420
She saw a man, but not a man, a demonic entity.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.940
Another hint that Michael is not a warlock
but possessed with the powers of Satan.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:46.880
John Henry thinks it might be a warning

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:52.160
and something in Cordelia's blood tells her the
only hope of surviving depends on what they do next.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.240
The reference to something in
her blood reminds me of episode 1,

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:00.940
where Timily - that's Timmy and Emily - were chosen
for the Outpost due to their exceptional genetics.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.020
Something tells me they'll be back.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:08.200
In two weeks' time, at the rise of the Blood Moon, Michael will be given the test of the Seven Wonders.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:13.000
The same test Zoey, Madison, Queenie
and Misty were given at the end of season 3.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.960
The Blood Moon is also interesting.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.560
The phenomenon whereby the moon in
total eclipse appears reddish in color.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:25.820
Across the globe, there have been reports of satanic or witchcraft rituals, which take place on this rare occasion.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.500
Myrtle decries Cordelia's
decision to let Michael perform the test,

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:35.100
reminding him that no male has ever succeeded
and if he passes, he will become the next Supreme.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:39.240
But let us remember, there have been
several clues to suggest he may not be male.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:43.720
Myrtle gives it to Cordelia, explaining
that the Alpha is merely a child's tale.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:47.280
Alpha being the legend told by Ariel of a male Supreme.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.240
She spurts how men have
caused pain throughout history,

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.860
referring to Attila the Hun, Herod the
Great and of course, Mark Zuckerberg.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:58.380
"Just a sec. Mom, could you get me my Frodo ring?"

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.220
Cordelia questions her own leadership. She's scared.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:05.500
What if it's her own hubris preventing
her from relinquishing her title to Michael?

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.300
Myrtle makes a good point: Passing the Seven
Wonders doesn't mean one is fit to lead the coven.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:15.180
She references Cordelia's mother Fiona, who
put her own vanity before that of the coven.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:18.160
She goes on to explain that
magic can be found anywhere.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.700
Take for example their star pupil, Mallory.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.740
Mallory heals a doe in the forest.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.740
Notice the gemstones in witch
symbology, like the moon on her rings.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:28.260
She also wears a crown,

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:32.260
the crown another subtle clue that
she's not a witch, but something more.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:36.900
While Michael possesses destructive power
gained by what is likely a demonic source,

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:40.940
could Mallory be the opposite,
the foil to Michael's Satanism?

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.620
Remember when he was communicating with
his father during the satanic ritual in episode 3

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:48.160
that he said he thought he killed them all.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:51.920
Was he referring to something
more than witches, perhaps angels?

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:56.340
Myrtle even explains that Mallory's powers
are unlike any magic she's ever seen.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.840
She asks Cordelia to delay the test, but
Cordelia tells her time is of the essence.

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:02.500
Her powers are fading.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.640
We see a gruesome wound on her
stomach and she tells Myrtle she's dying.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:10.800
Her fainting at the end of episode
4 is beginning to make more sense.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:15.560
Mallory interrupts this moment, again wearing
flowery gold trinkets and a crown of leaves,

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.780
similar to what rulers in Ancient
Rome like Caesar would wear.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:23.060
A subtle hint that at the end of this season,
she will take over Michael as Supreme.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.180
She informs Cordelia that an
appointment is waiting for her.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:31.240
It's Mr. Vanderbilt St. Pierre, Coco's father
who we saw get blown up in episode 1.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:35.320
He's thanking Cordelia for accepting
Coco, who is simply not having it.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:39.060
She feels she doesn't deserve to be
there because she has a shit power:

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.480
Gluten detector.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:45.040
Women from all over Beverly Hills
sought out Coco for her gluten detecting power.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:51.360
And let me just say, I thought it was absolutely hilarious that Princess Coco randomly has a pony in her backyard.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:56.540
Cordelia tries to quell Coco's fear, saying that
sensing danger in something is a good place to start,

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.220
but Coco brushes her off, saying,

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:02.720
"The only reason you're accepting me
is that my dad donated a zillion dollars."

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.440
Cordelia tasks Mallory with
showing her around the school,

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:09.000
and we get a better sense of how
these two came together in episode 1.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:14.660
Clearly Cordelia predicted the bomb going off, and
in order to protect the girls - likely from Langdon -,

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:17.240
placed a spell on them and hid them around the country.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:22.140
Remember in episode 1 when the plane had no
pilot and magically adjusted after the bomb blast

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:23.180
to avoid a crash?

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:24.640
Who was controlling that plane?

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:27.900
Likely Cordelia and the witches.
They've been watching over them.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.640
The warlocks perform a blessing on
Michael to prepare him for the test.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:36.880
You'll notice Ariel's adorned with three ornaments around his neck, not like the others who only have one.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:40.040
This is to denote his higher rank of Grand Chancellor.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:43.880
They put water, salt and blood into
a bowl and surround Michael with it,

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:46.960
igniting it in blue flame before performing their blessing,

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.340
referring to him as their champion.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.760
As Michael's congratulated, a mysterious wind blows in,

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:56.560
just like a wind blew away the
candles from Emily's room in episode 2.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.480
Which we know was also Michael's doing.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:01.060
John Henry catches a
glimpse of Michael's demonic form

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:03.980
and decides to get the hell
out of there to inform Cordelia.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:08.780
Behold tries to convince him to stay, but John
tells him he saw the white-faced man in Michael.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:12.780
They have a brief warlock battle,
John clearly the stronger magic user,

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:14.620
and we get this great line:

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.260
"Stand down, bitch."

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:19.900
On his way to visit Cordelia, John
stops for gas and meets Mead.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:22.820
My first instinct? This probably won't go over well.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:27.960
But since this is the past timeline, it's likely not
robot Mead, just Michael's satanic mother.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:33.580
Again, likely not his biological mother, since we may get more into that with Murder House around the corner.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.400
John makes the mistake of helping her

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:39.520
and she rewards him by slitting his
Achilles tendons and pouring gasoline on him.

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:41.440
What a mother won't do for her son.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:45.040
Michael meets with Mother in the
creepy forest and his plans are revealed.

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:50.660
His goal is to destroy the coven from within so that 
he may walk the path to what he was born to do.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.380
Mead reveals that Ariel was also in on the plan.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:57.660
He wouldn't want John Henry blowing their
chances of having the first male Supreme.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:01.380
But interesting that Mead says,
"Don't tell him about your father".

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:04.040
Ariel has a huge ax to grind with the witches.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:07.160
He's tired of being beholden to them, a second fiddle.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:08.960
He wants to make them squirm.

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:13.700
6 of the 7 Wonders are then presented in
an old-fashioned black-and-white montage.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.000
Telekinesis

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.000
Concilium

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.140
Transmutation

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:18.060
Divination

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:19.040
Pyrokinesis

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.720
and Vitalum Vitalis.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:23.080
Before the final and most arduous task:

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:23.900
Descensum

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:28.420
Cordelia tasks Michael with retrieving Misty,
who failed the test back in season 3.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:31.200
No other Supreme has ever been made to do this.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:33.440
Baldwin even states that it's suicide.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.120
Ariel is pissed at Cordelia.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.780
Michael should be tasked with doing exactly as she did.

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:42.800
But if Michael is to lead them in the times ahead,
their leader needs to be able to withstand anything.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:46.940
Ariel calls her out. She's fading, but
afraid to let go of her role as Supreme.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:52.320
She's just like her mother, Fiona, the former Supreme,
a weak, frightened woman clinging to power.

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:57.680
Cordelia, going full nuclear on Ariel, tells him
she can rip up his larynx with a flick of her finger.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.400
She's still Supreme, and he better fall in line.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.900
Michael interrupts and agrees to get Misty.

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:07.320
The witches and warlocks surround Michael
as he begins the final test, Descensum.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:08.440
He chants in Latin.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:14.900
Now, my Latin is not that good but it roughly translates to "Lead me in the dark at the end of life to greet Hell".

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:19.360
Michael walks down a black hallway,
which I get a big Hotel Cortez vibe from,

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:23.120
as we witness Misty bringing
back to life a frog in biology class,

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:28.060
likely having to relive over and over a
traumatic experience from her past.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:33.400
Her own personal Hell, kind of like what Madison
was doing in episode 4 at the department store.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:38.200
The teacher makes her kill the live frog, and Michael saves her by stabbing the teacher with a scalpel.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.580
Man, school has changed since I was a kid.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.580
Michael awakens, the witches and
warlocks thinking Misty was not saved,

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:46.840
that is, until she reappears.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.840
Cordelia and Misty reunite,

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:54.520
Myrtle saying she's back from a state of perdition,
often referred to as the final state of damnation.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:59.140
After a brief moment of happiness, Michael
seems to use his powers to make Cordelia bleed,

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:01.760
Misty being the only one to notice this.

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:05.660
Apparently, after a new Supreme
is reached, the old one fades away.

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:09.800
Whether Ariel is being literal here or
simply her powers fade is uncertain.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:13.720
The witches and warlocks argue before
Cordelia raises her voice exclaiming,

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:17.360
"There can be no doubt. Michael is the next Supreme."

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:18.760
before she faints again.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.300
Cordelia recovers and Misty brings her soup.

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:25.720
She says she should have left her where
she was. Michael gives her the heebie-jeebies.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:29.880
We flash back to when Misty was in Hell
and learn that after Michael killed the teacher,

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:34.040
he somehow communicated to the
kids who were speaking in gibberish.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.360
Misty says evil was speaking to him.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:38.540
Was he talking to Satan himself?

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:42.520
Cordelia doesn't believe it. Perhaps
he was negotiating her release from Hell.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:46.040
Misty could always sense evil
as a child, smell rotting souls.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:51.040
But she's never smelled anything like Michael,
describing it as the "perfume of death".

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:55.640
Myrtle demands that he not become
Supreme and Cordelia surprisingly agrees.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.800
This was all a plan by
Cordelia to gauge his powers.

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:02.900
As the old saying goes, "Keep your
friends close and your enemies closer."

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:06.480
A lesson from Niccolò Machiavelli,
who, in his book "The Prince",

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.700
provides a primer for how
to become an effective dictator.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.880
Cordelia once again reminds
them that something is coming.

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:18.100
But this time Michael has given them an advantage:
He's brought all her girls back for the fight ahead.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:22.840
But she says something really interesting
here: that Misty brought back the first proof.

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:25.720
What is she referring to?
The proof that he's demonic?

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:28.720
And if there are more proofs,
who will they have to present it to?

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:32.120
The witches celebrate when
Stevie Nicks, the White Witch, joins.

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:35.620
Her being a member of
Fleetwood Mac sings their song "Gypsy",

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:41.040
a song which she wrote to remind her of her life
before she was famous, a song to humble her.

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:43.460
The term "gypsy" can also mean two things:

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:47.520
a member of a traveling people
traditionally living by trade and fortune telling,

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:50.300
and also a nomadic or free spirited person.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:54.960
Madison is tasked by Cordelia to travel
and find everything she can about Michael,

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.860
because of the danger he poses.

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:58.860
Could she be tasked to finding more proof?

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:00.500
But they're eavesdropped by Behold.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:04.300
He says if they're going to dig up dirt, he
should come along, or he'll tell Michael.

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:07.980
He won't go to Michael directly
because he has a bad gut feeling about him.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.660
But this is quite a change of character

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:13.060
from what we saw earlier when he
tried to stop John Henry from leaving.

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:16.580
This leads me to believe that
Behold will be a spy working for Michael,

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.680
keeping tabs on Madison and the witches.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.860
After all, we did just see him eavesdrop.

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:24.000
Cordelia agrees to the arrangement
and gives them their destination:

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:26.000
Season One's Murder House.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:27.180
Now, this is huge.

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:32.280
We knew Murder House was going to be featured, but how it would be integrated into the story was unknown.

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:36.580
But for now, it looks like it's going to play a role
in learning more about how Michael came to be.

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:42.140
We know he was the child of Vivien and Tate from season 1 and taken in by Jessica Lange's character.

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:44.060
What mysteries will this house hold

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:48.680
and what new information will it give the witches
that may lead to finding out Michael's weakness?

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:50.360
Could it be his real mother?

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:53.700
Not to mention how this all
ties in to the eventual apocalypse.

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:57.060
Remember, this episode didn't
touch on any of the present timeline,

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:00.940
where Michael confronts Cordelia and
the newly arisen witches in the Outpost.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:05.840
My guess is the next episode or even next
couple will focus solely on the past timeline,

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:08.740
and eventually lead to where we left off in episode 4.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:10.240
That's it for this episode.

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:11.740
Make sure to like and subscribe.

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:14.840
I have a new Twitter account where
you can find out when I release my videos,

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:17.200
or if you just want to cast a witch spell on me.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:18.580
Until next time.

